\title{zulm: Tensor Graphs, Training and Inference on 'ggml'}
\description{
Builds computation graphs of tensors in R, runs them on the CPU, differentiates them and trains their parameters, through the 'ggml' tensor library (\url{https://github.com/ggml-org/ggml}) bundled in its CPU subset. Graphs are built once per input shape and run many times; the same operations train small and medium neural networks with the AdamW and SGD optimisers and run pretrained transformer checkpoints read from 'GGUF' or 'safetensors' files. Results reproduce bit for bit at a fixed seed whatever the thread count. A versioned C interface lets other packages build models on top.
